title: MackenzieJoyceClue0
---
On a cloudy afternoon, Mackenzie walked her small, stubborn beagle mix, Charlie, who pulled tight at the leash as he strained to follow a scent. As she pulled the dog along, she glanced around and noticed that the familiar trail she walked nearly every day was unusually empty and unnervingly quiet. Suddenly a tornado siren pierced through the eerie calm, and Mackenzie crumpled to the ground and covered her ears. Charlie circled around her, whimpering and then howling up at the siren mounted on a pole several feet over their heads.  It shook her bones and vibrated every organ in her body. She curled into a protective ball and rocked herself back and forth. When she realized it wouldn’t stop, she yanked off her jacket and wrapped it around her head to block the violent noise, forcing herself back onto her feet. With Charlie pulling toward home, they raced away under the darkening sky.  
===

title: MackenzieJoyceClue1
---
At a sleepway camp during the summer Mackenzie turned fifteen,, she awoke suddenly in the middle of the night. Everything looked blurry and strange, like she was wearing red-tinted goggles. She looked down and saw her once white pajama shirt was now soaked through with dark, sticky blood. She screamed and grabbed her face. The blood was coming from everywhere. Nose. Eyes. Ears. Her gurgled screams woke her roommate, who scrambled to the camp counselor’s cot to bring back help.. Mackenzie came in and out of consciousness, until she finally resurfacing in a hospital bed. The massive nosebleed had filled and overflowed her sinuses while she slept, forcing her to wake in a pool of her own blood. She did go back to camp and tried to pass it off to her friends as just a weird fluke. But she feared falling asleep every single night.
===
title: MackenzieJoyceClue2
---
On her eighteenth birthday, Mackenzie went out early to walk her dog. Her family had a whole day of activities planned,  but she needed some time to herself before the craziness began. While walking on a poorly maintained part of the trail, Charlie stopped and stared at a bush that separated twisted brush from the gravel path. Suddenly, a snarling black dog shot out of the brush, white foam coming through its bared teeth. The dog lunged at Charlie. Mackenzie screamed and turned to run, pulling hard on the leash to drag Charlie away. But in the next second, the attacker had sunk its teeth into Charlie’s pink abdomen, violently shaking him back and forth. The last rush of air that left Charlie’s lungs created a sharp, agonized bark that reverberated through the trees. The last thing Mackznie saw before running for help that wouldn’t come in time was her beloved beagle’s body covered in blood tinged with white foam. 
===